## DATASETS

### Usage_df (weekly_usage.csv)
20,868,730 rows, 4 columns:
- PANELISTID         : Unique user identifier (join key to User_df)
- WEEK               : Start date of observation week (weekly aggregation Mon-Sun)
- APPDESCRIPTION     : Name of the mobile app used
- FOREGROUNDDURATION : Weekly cumulative app usage — confirmed in MINUTES
                       Aggregated from session-level records (open to close)
                       Values above 10,080 minutes are impossible (minutes in a week)
                       Use IQR method or top 1-5% percentile for outlier detection

### User_df (user_info.csv)
11,793 rows, 10 columns:
- PANELISTID  : Unique user identifier (join key to Usage_df)
- AGE         : User age (numeric, has ~295 missing values)
- GENDER      : Male / Female / Unknown (114 Unknown users identified)
- CITY        : User city and state
- TREATED     : 1 = used an AI/LLM app, 0 = control group (never used AI app)
- Weekday     : Average DAILY app usage on weekdays (Mon-Fri) — in minutes
- Weekend     : Average DAILY app usage on weekends (Sat-Sun) — in minutes
- Morning     : Average app usage during 6am-11am — in minutes, daily average
- Afternoon   : Average app usage during 12pm-5pm — in minutes, daily average
- Night       : Average app usage during 6pm-5am — in minutes, daily average

IMPORTANT: Weekday/Weekend and Morning/Afternoon/Night are DAILY AVERAGES not 
weekly totals. They are independent measures and cannot be summed to equal each 
other. Do not treat them as additive.

